[{:db/id 17592186192855 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-838db218-c7b5-5ab1-b5e1-0abd38558574" "question-5b9ce7e4-46a6-59bd-8550-ab45a107e732"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192614 :question/worked-solution "![](images/eb/ebebd8b07b11592683a280b53674fa5a153743830f833e752b5b16df1bbf809d.png)\n\nTwo lines are parallel if they never intersect.\n\nIn the given diagram, the only parallel lines are $l$ and $m.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192729 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-098eea8f-65a3-53e7-b532-eec2a5a08b22" "question-1f0a9542-3ba4-5c20-945c-8b2a173ef94b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192442 :question/worked-solution "![](images/35/3528edd920ddd50e0e976a46a78980708369f17f5809a3b8578af1bda683fc8b.png)\n\nTwo lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a $90^\\circ$ angle.\n\nIn the given diagram, the only perpendicular lines are $p$ and $q.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192728 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b26db26d-7241-5602-a20a-a5953a1b2569" "question-2d6731a9-4b1d-5a58-8690-9d08ea615462" "question-e371cbf5-7ac9-5e8f-8f0f-f99fbc339fe5" "question-86e173f6-09d0-539e-96a4-71b8b3120bde" "question-f045e30a-5c77-5aee-853f-bedc4016f900"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192441 :question/worked-solution "Two lines are parallel if they never intersect.\n\nFirst, notice that the lines $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{PQ}$ and  $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{TS}$ are parallel.\n\n![](images/78/783488aa5e48aac72fe8aa4870f9a3e5621799475286bcc820573ae099b3ed6b.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overline{PQ}$ and $\\overline{TS}$ are parallel. We can write this as follows: \n\n$$\n\\overline{PQ} \\parallel \\overline{TS}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-838db218-c7b5-5ab1-b5e1-0abd38558574" :question/id #uuid "838db218-c7b5-5ab1-b5e1-0abd38558574" :question/math-academy-id "q-153263" :question/problem "![](images/de/de307da2bc912e9eb6f7312a16be40908d6ccd43cbc613367d042ed55090f2ee.png)\n\nGiven the diagram above, which of the following statements is true?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $p$ and $q$ are two lines. Then,\n\n- $p∥q$ means $p$ and $q$ are parallel, and\n\n- $p⊥q$ means $p$ and $q$ are perpendicular.\n\nThe lines $a,c$ and $b,d$ are parallel since they will never intersect. Therefore, the correct statement is $a∥c$ and $b∥d.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d280ef1a-3278-51d3-8ac5-974e454c72d5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d280ef1a-3278-51d3-8ac5-974e454c72d5" :answer-field/id #uuid "d280ef1a-3278-51d3-8ac5-974e454c72d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5cc39b58-cdc8-581a-9b94-9526789c6036" :answer-field/choices ["answer-14132441-2fcd-5f99-8612-71fa0ff59eaa" "answer-5582d200-52be-5108-8fd2-4b7733446344" "answer-5cc39b58-cdc8-581a-9b94-9526789c6036" "answer-1a389dcc-5890-524a-98d4-5b2f9ede21b2" "answer-c4f16f70-2339-58fd-a081-ee1918167f6a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14132441-2fcd-5f99-8612-71fa0ff59eaa" :answer/id #uuid "14132441-2fcd-5f99-8612-71fa0ff59eaa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q∥a$ and $Q∥b$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5582d200-52be-5108-8fd2-4b7733446344" :answer/id #uuid "5582d200-52be-5108-8fd2-4b7733446344" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q⊥a$ and $Q⊥b$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cc39b58-cdc8-581a-9b94-9526789c6036" :answer/id #uuid "5cc39b58-cdc8-581a-9b94-9526789c6036" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a∥c$ and $b∥d$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a389dcc-5890-524a-98d4-5b2f9ede21b2" :answer/id #uuid "1a389dcc-5890-524a-98d4-5b2f9ede21b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a⊥b$ and $c∥d$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4f